# The file manager's icon view (`v`): a folder, a text file, a sound and a
# picture with its thumbnail. At 800x600 the window's content is 640x400 at
# 38,62: five cells of 112 pixels from x=78, from y=84; the icons are
# 64x64 at 24,6 in their cell.
@cpus 4
@ai
$ ai control on
$ display mode 800x600
~ ^mode: 800x600
$ mkdir /p
$ mkdir /p/box
$ echo hello > /p/a.txt
$ tune save /p/s.wav c5
saved 1 notes to /p/s.wav (47 KiB)
$ screenshot /p/shot.png
~ ^saved the screen \(800 x 600\) to /p/shot\.png
$ files /p
/p in a new window: arrows choose, Enter opens, q leaves
@ctl keys {machine} "v"
$ sleep 1
# The chosen cell, the folder, the page, the sound, the thumbnail's frame,
# and the background below the icons.
@screenshot 800x600 pixels 82,86=3a6ea5 132,120=f2c14e 228,95=f4f4f4 336,100=4a3a6a 437,97=d0d0d0 43,362=1c2230
# Arrows move in the grid; Enter on the picture opens the viewer.
@ctl keys {machine} "{right}{right}{right}{enter}"
$ sleep 1
$ threads
~ view +(waiting|ready)
@ctl keys {machine} "q"
$ sleep 1
# Back to the list: the bar is still on the picture.
@ctl keys {machine} "v"
@ctl text {machine}
~ ^ /p  \(4 of 4\)$
~ ^   <folder>  box/$
@ctl keys {machine} "q"
$ sleep 1
$ threads
!~ files
